{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:PredictedSpectra.IntegerStability","@type":"LeanModule","name":"PredictedSpectra.IntegerStability","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.integer_stability_strict","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.integer_stability_strict","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/integer-stability.lean#L59-L70","doc":"Strict version: away from the vertex the binding energy is strictly larger,\nwhich is what makes the integer minimiser one of the two nearest integers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.integer_stability","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.integer_stability","kind":"theorem","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/integer-stability.lean#L43-L57","doc":"**Convex-quadratic stability of the proton number.**\n\nFor `α > 0` the binding energy `E(p) = α p² − γ p + δ` attains its global\nminimum at the continuous optimum `p* = γ/(2α)`, i.e. `E(p*) ≤ E(p)` for\nevery real `p`, with equality iff `p = p*`.  Strict convexity then forces the\ninteger minimiser to lie in `{⌊p*⌋, ⌈p*⌉}` — the exactness asserted in the\nnarrative statement. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:integer-stability","label":"prop:integer-stability","md":"quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/integer-stability.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bindingEnergy_vertex_form","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bindingEnergy_vertex_form","kind":"theorem","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/integer-stability.lean#L34-L41","doc":"**Completing the square.**  `E(p) = α (p − p*)² + (δ − γ²/4α)`, exhibiting the\nvertex of the parabola at `p* = γ/(2α)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.continuousOptimum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.continuousOptimum","kind":"def","line":31,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/integer-stability.lean#L31-L32","doc":"The continuous optimum `p*(A) = γ / (2 α)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bindingEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bindingEnergy","kind":"def","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/predicted-spectra/integer-stability.lean#L27-L29","doc":"The binding energy as a function of the proton number `p` at fixed mass\nnumber, `E(p) = α p² − γ p + δ` (`def:stable-nucleus`). ","signatureChunk":0}]}